      "Looking for that ideal getaway exploring a natural wonderland while experiencing an authentically preserved historic western town brimming with cuisine, charming shops and arts?",
      "Book a trip to rejuvenate among the breathtaking vistas and rich arts and culinary culture of Livingston Montana, the year round and historic gateway to Yellowstone National Park.",
      "Livingston is picturesque town nestled on the Yellowstone River among four stunning mountain ranges. Historic downtown gives authentic old west movie set vibes with brick storefronts and vintage neon signs, but with vibrant businesses humming with art and activities.",
      "Winter is the ideal time to visit Yellowstone National Park and the surrounding wilderness areas. The crowds are gone, lodging and restaurants are relaxed and quiet, and wildlife is performing their seasonal rituals. It’s like your own private winter wonderland snow globe. Local’s favorite winter recreation includes; cross country skiing or snowshoeing, dog sled rides, ice skating, and soaking in outdoor Paradise Valley hot springs.",
      "Hungry after an invigorating day outdoors? Livingston’s culinary scene is exceptional; creative farm to table cuisine, elevated wild game dishes, indulgent Italian classics, European style bakeries, rustic steak and burger joints, ethnic food, vintage cafés, a dozen small coffee shops, diverse bars, and two breweries. Sample as many dishes as possible during the annual Winter Restaurant Week, and enjoy seasonal and holiday specials at unique eateries and gourmet markets.",
      "Livingston hosts 50 old-fashioned holiday events and markets ranging from; Holiday Lights festival, Skate with Santa, Craft and Arts Markets, Christmas Stroll, Santa’s Village, and live Holiday Vaudeville Theatre. There’s live music nearly every night, and literary and arts events weekly. Step back in history at Livingston's Yellowstone Gateway history museum.",
      "Treasure hunt in downtown boutiques to score vintage, handcrafted and upcycled bespoke goods, records and books, handmade jams, gifts and toys galore, snazzy western wear and practical winter gear, unique art – and you will likely meet the business owner or maker in person as all Downtown businesses are small, independent and locally owned.",
